# Polyburg.com robots.txt
#
# SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for crawler rules. Next.js can also generate a
# robots.txt from src/app/robots.ts, but a static public/robots.txt always
# wins — so robots.ts was DELETED (2026-08-18) to stop the two from
# diverging. Edit THIS file only; do not re-add src/app/robots.ts.
#
# Each User-agent record below is complete (its own Allow/Disallow lines) —
# per the robots spec, a bot matches exactly one record, so every record
# must carry the full rule set it needs.

